/-!
# Serre's global generation theorem for ample line bundles

Let `X` be a quasi-separated scheme, `a` an ample line-bundle class on `X`
(`LineBundleClass.IsAmple`), and `F` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type. Then there is a
bound `n₀ : ℕ` such that for every `n ≥ n₀` and every invertible sheaf `M` representing `aⁿ`, the
twist `F ⊗ M` is generated by finitely many global sections
(`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_generatingSections_tensor`). No Noetherian hypothesis on `X` is
needed.

The proof follows the standard two-step argument (Hartshorne, Theorem II.5.17; Stacks, Tag 01Q3):

1. When an invertible sheaf `L` already carries finitely many global sections whose nonvanishing
   loci `X_{sᵢ}` are affine and cover `X`, each affine open `X_{sᵢ}` has finitely many generators
   of `Γ(F, X_{sᵢ})`. By `Scheme.Modules.exists_map_eq_tmulRight_tensorPowSection`, after tensoring
   with a power of `sᵢ` each generator extends to a global section of `F ⊗ Lⁿ`. Taking `n₀` to be
   the maximum of these exponents and tensoring further with powers of `sᵢ` yields, for every
   `n ≥ n₀`, finitely many global sections of `F ⊗ Lⁿ` whose restrictions span `Γ(F ⊗ Lⁿ, X_{sᵢ})`
   on each chart (`Scheme.Modules.bijective_tmulRight_tensorPowSection_of_le_nonvanishingLocus`).
   By the affine-cover criterion (`Scheme.Modules.epi_freeHomEquiv_symm_of_span_eq_top`), these
   sections globally generate `F ⊗ Lⁿ`.
2. For an arbitrary ample class `a`, quasi-compactness provides a finite affine cover by
   nonvanishing loci of global sections of positive powers `a^{dᵢ}`. Raising each section to the
   power `m / dᵢ` for `m = ∏ dᵢ` (which preserves the nonvanishing locus by
   `Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection`) produces finitely many global sections of a
   single positive power `Lᵐ` whose affine nonvanishing loci cover `X`
   (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_pow_iSup_nonvanishingLocus_eq_top`). Applying the first step to
   the finitely many residue twists `F ⊗ Lʳ` (`0 ≤ r < m`) yields the uniform bound for all
   `n ≥ n₀`.

As consequences:

* For any invertible sheaf `K`, the twists `K ⊗ M` are globally generated for `n ≥ n₀`
  (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct`).
* Tensoring a surjection `𝒪_X^k ↠ F ⊗ M` with an inverse `K` (`M ⊗ K ≅ 𝒪_X`) gives an epimorphism
  from a finite direct sum `K^⊕k ↠ F` (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_epi_biproduct`).

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01PR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PR) and
  [Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3).
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory BraidedCategory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
